1
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:04,840
Okay, are you ready?

2
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,052
There's nothing in here.

3
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:20,310
Hey, wait!

4
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:21,520
I'll be okay.

5
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,311
I'm not going in too far.

6
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,757
Besides, we should find out what
kind of boss we're dealing with.

7
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:28,657
How else are we gonna
figure out how to beat it?

8
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:29,720
Yeah, I know.

9
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,000
It's just...

10
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,117
I'm not sure what it is.

11
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:08,320
I've recognized that a terrible past,

12
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:14,700
I can't understand the
fact that I'm afraid.

13
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:17,740
I'm afraid of my back-to-face,

14
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:21,900
but I'm still in the future.

15
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:24,760
Thank you.

16
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:52,980
Oh, my!

17
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,120
I'm going to spread out.

18
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,997
I'm going to feel the weak of you,
I'm going to feel the weak of you!

19
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:04,577
I'm going to be strong in the world.

20
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:14,157
I want to always be waiting.

21
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:17,140
I'm giving everything I have.

22
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:36,220
That one's gonna be tough
to beat. You're right.

23
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:40,897
I saw you only had that one big sword, and
I'm pretty sure it's got special attacks,

24
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:41,810
too.

25
00:02:41,893 --> 00:02:43,477
We're gonna have to put
tanks in the front row

26
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:46,148
and keep switching out
just to wear it down.

27
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:49,377
Yeah, and it wouldn't hurt to
have about ten shield users.

28
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:50,780
Shield users, huh?

29
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:53,620
What? What's wrong? You are.

30
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,857
You're hiding something, aren't you?

31
00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:57,528
What are you talking about?

32
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,169
I just realized something.

33
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:03,737
The biggest advantage of using a one-handed
sword is you can also use a shield.

34
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:04,650
But you know what?

35
00:03:04,733 --> 00:03:07,209
I don't think I've ever
seen you using one.

36
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:10,815
I don't use a shield because
it'll slow down my rapier.

37
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:13,726
Others don't because
they think it looks dumb.

38
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:19,162
And how come you're not using the
sword you commissioned from Liz?

39
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,660
Very suspicious.

40
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:30,620
Oh, never mind.

41
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:34,324
It's rude to ask people
to justify their skills.

42
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:39,433
Since it's gotten so late,
might as well have lunch here.

43
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:41,210
Really?

44
00:03:41,293 --> 00:03:42,371
Did you make it yourself?

45
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,190
Yep.

46
00:03:44,273 --> 00:03:46,257
But you better take your
gloves off before you eat.

47
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:47,240
Oh, sure.

48
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:49,740
Here you go.

49
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:57,440
This is good.

50
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:02,116
How'd you get it to taste so amazing?

51
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:05,621
Chalk it up to a whole
year of training and study.

52
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,617
Aincrad has everything you need.

53
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:09,697
There's about a hundred
different seasonings.

54
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:11,937
I made everything just
by calculating all the

55
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:14,657
parameters used by the
flavor recreation engine.

56
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:18,269
This was made with grokwa seed,
sugar leaf, and calum water.

57
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:20,897
It's mayonnaise.

58
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:25,440
And I made this using abilba seed,
sag leaves, and oolah fish bone.

59
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:32,940
Whoa, that tastes exactly like soy sauce!

60
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,217
You're right, I made the sauce
for the sandwich out of that.

61
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:40,137
Amazing, it's perfect.

62
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:43,297
Have you thought about selling
this because you'd make a fortune?

63
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:44,851
You think it's that good?

64
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,740
Wait, you can't sell it

65
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:49,760
But, why not?

66
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,271
Because there wouldn't be any left for me.

67
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:58,000
My god, you're so greedy.

68
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:02,400
If you like it that much,
I could always make more.

69
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,880
Hey, Kirito!

70
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:17,335
How you doing, buddy?

71
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:21,020
Hey, Klein.

72
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:22,380
Still alive, huh?

73
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:24,620
Jeez, you're the same as ever.

74
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,150
Wait.

75
00:05:26,233 --> 00:05:28,220
Whoa, you're a solo player.

76
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,297
What the heck are you doing with a...

77
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:31,210
girl?

78
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:37,177
Uh, um, I could have sworn you guys
met before at one of the boss fights.

79
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:38,378
I'll introduce you.

80
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,892
This is Klein of the Foo-Rin Kazan Guild.

81
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:44,440
And this is Asuna of the
Knights of the Blood Oath.

82
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:48,580
Hey, come on, say something.

83
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:49,570
What's wrong?

84
00:05:49,653 --> 00:05:50,483
You lagging?

85
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:54,980
Hi, I'm Klein.

86
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,360
I'm 24 and single and looking for...

87
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:02,530
Boss!

88
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:10,950
Whoa!

89
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,727
Are you really that awesome?

90
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,680
Don't worry, it's cool.

91
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,136
These guys are okay.

92
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,799
Yeah, but I don't know about Klein.

93
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,320
What the hell?

94
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:26,580
That's payback, you weasel.

95
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:27,940
Come on, Klein.

96
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:29,737
What are you doing with a girl?

97
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:31,140
Holding out on me.

98
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,940
What's the deal, man? Spill it.

99
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:38,880
Uh, well... Excuse me.

100
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:42,557
Kirito and I are together
because we're sort of in a party.

101
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,470
Huh?

102
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:44,610
Huh?

103
00:06:44,693 --> 00:06:45,523
Kirito, you son of a...

104
00:06:45,606 --> 00:06:47,125
Wait, it's not what you think.

105
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:50,370
Kirito.

106
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,280
What the hell?

107
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:55,880
It's an army.

108
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:59,292
That's the big guild that runs floor one.

109
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:01,240
What are they doing up here?

110
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:04,052
They were almost slaughtered on floor 25.

111
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,157
Instead of clearing levels, they've
been trying to build up their numbers.

112
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:10,181
I haven't seen them on the
front lines in a while.

113
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,520
At ease!

114
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:25,440
I'm with the Aincrad Liberation
Army, Lieutenant Colonel Korvats.

115
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:27,560
I'm Kirito, Solo.

116
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:29,677
Sure you are.

117
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,517
Have you cleared the area up ahead?

118
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,430
Yeah.

119
00:07:32,513 --> 00:07:35,420
We also got a map with
directions to the boss room.

120
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:37,610
Hmm.

121
00:07:37,693 --> 00:07:38,523
Right.

122
00:07:38,606 --> 00:07:40,504
Then hand over that map
and we'll be on our way.

123
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:43,379
You want us to just give it to you?

124
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:46,715
You even know how much of a
pain in the ass mapping is?

125
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:51,213
We share our information and resources
with civilian players all the time!

126
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:53,417
And we don't charge a thing for it!

127
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:56,280
We maintain order in the chaos of battle,

128
00:07:56,500 --> 00:08:00,265
so that all players can leave
this world as quickly as possible!

129
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:03,740
Therefore, it's your duty
to cooperate with us!

130
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,134
So hand over that map!

131
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:07,440
Listen, you!

132
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,180
You bastard! Easy.

133
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:13,417
When we got back to town, I was going
to go public with the map anyway.

134
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:16,337
It's cool. Oh, now wait. Come on, man.

135
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:17,997
You're being way too nice to him.

136
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,727
I don't care about making
money off map data.

137
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,493
Thanks for cooperating.

138
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:32,897
By the way, if you're planning to hit
the boss, I wouldn't recommend it.

139
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:34,760
That is my decision to make.

140
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:39,097
Hey, I just took a look
inside that room, pal.

141
00:08:39,180 --> 00:08:42,592
And you can't beat that boss
if your troops are half dead.

142
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:43,860
Look at them.

143
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,079
They're exhausted.

144
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:46,790
Nonsense.

145
00:08:46,873 --> 00:08:48,097
My men are tougher than that.

146
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:50,040
They won't quit until I say so.

147
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,600
On your feet.

148
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:52,720
Come on, move.

149
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,260
Oh, man.

150
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:03,822
Are those guys going to be okay?

151
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,757
I'm sure they know what they're doing.

152
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:09,487
They won't rush the boss without
checking it out first, right?

153
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:12,331
Maybe we should keep an eye on him anyway.

154
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,520
I don't know who's nicer, you or me.

155
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:32,060
So, anyway, Asuna, I got a favor to ask.

156
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:37,020
He can be hard to talk to, and he's
a loner and addicted to combat,

157
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,860
but he's a good guy.

158
00:09:39,180 --> 00:09:40,709
Take care of him, will ya?

159
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:46,930
Okay.

160
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:49,985
I promise, he's in good hands.

161
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:01,717
That's the last one.

162
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,800
Only thing left's the boss's room.

163
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:07,921
Maybe those guys used some kind of
teleportation thingy to go back.

164
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:12,250
Asuna!

165
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,180
Ray!

166
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,330
Idiots!

167
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:26,100
Hey!

168
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:27,440
You guys okay?

169
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,033
Don't just stand there!

170
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:42,720
Use your teleport crystals! We can't!

171
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:44,667
The crystals aren't working!

172
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:50,424
I've never heard of a trap like
this being in a boss room before.

173
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:56,520
The Uncrant Liberation Army
doesn't know the word retreat!

174
00:10:56,940 --> 00:10:57,820
Come on!

175
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:00,300
Keep fighting! They're insane.

176
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:02,680
Hey, what the hell's going on?

177
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,868
They can't use their
teleportation crystals.

178
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:09,137
We could distract the boss, but
going in there is too risky.

179
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:11,840
But isn't there something we can do?

180
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:19,470
Ready?

181
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:22,390
CHARGE!

182
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,420
Don't do it!

183
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:44,410
Hey!

184
00:11:44,493 --> 00:11:45,800
Hang on, Korvats.

185
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:56,100
I can't believe it.

186
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:01,860
No.

187
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,300
No.

188
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:15,240
I can't.

189
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:16,680
No.

190
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:28,520
Oh, what the hell?

191
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:51,560
Get out!

192
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:55,400
I got you, buddy.

193
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,180
Thanks.

194
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:13,700
This'll take forever.

195
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,000
Get out of there! Kirito!

196
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,713
The only way to end this is if I use it.

197
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:31,890
But then...

198
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:50,930
Damn it!

199
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,196
Just use it already!

200
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,320
Hey, Klein! Asuna! Listen!

201
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:56,597
I need ten seconds!

202
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:57,621
Keep him off me!

203
00:13:58,640 --> 00:13:59,960
Yeah, you got it!

204
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,100
Okay, I'm ready!

205
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,060
Switch out!

206
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:42,880
Okay, here goes.

207
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:44,900
Starburst stream!

208
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,318
What the hell kind of skill is that?

209
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:56,630
Faster!

210
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:07,641
Gotta go faster!

211
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:37,140
Is it...

212
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:39,530
over?

213
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:07,930
Kirito!

214
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,540
Wake up, Kirito!

215
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,420
Oh, man, my head.

216
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:28,817
That was too close.

217
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,440
How long was I out for?

218
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:31,820
Just a few seconds.

219
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:34,060
You reckless!

220
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:35,450
Eddie!

221
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,700
Jeez, don't hug me so hard.

222
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:41,920
I'll lose the last of my HP.

223
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:48,985
Korvats and two of his men are
the only ones who didn't make it.

224
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:54,580
We haven't lost a player in
a boss fight since Floor 67.

225
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:56,997
That wasn't a boss fight.

226
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,080
That was suicide.

227
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:00,500
Korvats was a damn fool.

228
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:04,249
There's no point to
any of this if you die.

229
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,557
You're not off the hook either.

230
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:13,640
What the hell did you do just now?

231
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:16,184
I don't think you want to know.

232
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,540
Oh, come on!

233
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:20,231
I've never seen anything like that before!

234
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,462
It's an extra skill I picked up.

235
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:25,200
Dual wielding.

236
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:28,345
Dude, are there prerequisites?

237
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:31,111
If I knew that, I'd have shared it by now.

238
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:34,000
It's not on the Infobroker skill list.

239
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,167
Guess it's exclusive to you.

240
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:38,067
Hey, you got a unique skill.

241
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:40,558
Way to stay on the down low, Kirito.

242
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:43,617
How can you keep an awesome secret
like this from your buddies?

243
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:49,097
About six months ago, I was scrolling
through my skill menu, and it was just...

244
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:50,010
there.

245
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,440
Dual wielding.

246
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:55,937
But if anyone else found out
I had a skill like this...

247
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:58,657
They'd get pissed because you
had something they didn't.

248
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:00,975
Some gamers are like that, but not me.

249
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:02,150
You're right, though.

250
00:18:02,233 --> 00:18:04,577
People would definitely
be jealous you had that.

251
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:05,490
And that.

252
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:11,237
Well, they say your character's
built by life's challenges,

253
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:13,380
so keep soldiering on, young man.

254
00:18:15,580 --> 00:18:16,880
Easier said than done.

255
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:21,317
We're gonna go trigger the warp gate.

256
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:22,230
You coming?

257
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:25,657
Nah, I'll catch up with you later.

258
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:27,093
Need to rest for a bit.

259
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:28,890
I heard that.

260
00:18:28,973 --> 00:18:30,094
Have a safe trip back.

261
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:36,980
Oh, and by the way... Huh?

262
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:39,297
You know how you ran in there?

263
00:18:39,380 --> 00:18:41,674
To rescue those army guys like you did?

264
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:43,510
Yeah.

265
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:50,397
Well, you know, I'm glad you did.

266
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,656
Anyway, I'll see ya.

267
00:18:59,140 --> 00:19:00,316
What's wrong, Asuna?

268
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:03,957
I was so scared.

269
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:06,720
If you died, I didn't know what I'd do.

270
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:09,028
What are you talking about?

271
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:11,927
You're the one who jumped
in first, remember?

272
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:19,180
I'm taking a leave of absence from the
guild. Why? And do what? Sleep in all day?

273
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:21,220
Did you forget already?

274
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:23,660
I said I was teaming up with you.

275
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:12,877
A blue demon that annihilated a
big squad of army guys and a 50

276
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:16,725
-hit combo from a dual wielder
who took out the boss by himself.

277
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:21,084
I can't believe what a big deal
they're making out of this thing.

278
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:24,237
Yeah, it's blowing up right in my face.

279
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:28,297
A buttload of swordsmen and info brokers
showed up at my place this morning.

280
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:31,117
Now I need a new pad because
they know where I live.

281
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:34,141
Yeah, well, that's sort
of kind of your own fault.

282
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:36,437
You said it was going
to be our little secret,

283
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:38,873
but you went and blabbed it to everyone.

284
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:49,337
What are we gonna do, Kirito?

285
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:54,597
We've got ourselves a huge
problem outside of boss fights.

286
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:57,817
I don't believe we've
ever actually met, Kirito.

287
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:01,837
Well, there was that
conference on floor 67.

288
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:03,717
We talked a little bit there.

289
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,617
Commander Heathcliff.

290
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:08,977
Yes, that was a difficult
battle, wasn't it?

291
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:11,517
We almost lost a few players there too.

292
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:16,657
We may be the top guild, but we barely
get by with the amount of troops we have.

293
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:20,777
And now here you are trying to
poach one of our best players.

294
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:22,880
I don't know what to say.

295
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:28,217
If she's that important, maybe you should
do a better job picking her bodyguard.

296
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:32,997
You have my sincerest apologies for any
trouble you might have had with Kuradeel.

297
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:35,157
But you must understand
that we simply cannot

298
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:37,317
allow our second in
command to leave the guild,

299
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,337
just like that.

300
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:44,897
If you want her, you'll have to use
your dual blades to take her from us.

301
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:49,077
If you can defeat me in combat,
you'll be free to take Asuna with you.

302
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:54,260
On the other hand, if you lose, you
will join the Knights of the Blood Oath.

303
00:21:58,540 --> 00:21:59,370
Yeah, okay.

304
00:21:59,453 --> 00:22:02,237
If you want to settle this
with swords, that's fine by me.

305
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:04,560
We'll have ourselves a duel then.

306
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:20,240
What did you hear?

307
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:24,037
The last one you saw on the morning...

308
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:25,337
I was very frozen to the night.

309
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:26,250
When I hear you, the
sound of a little cold.

310
00:22:26,333 --> 00:22:30,257
It's a little late for you to
come to the light. I hear you.

311
00:22:30,340 --> 00:22:31,170
My heart's at a little bit more,

312
00:22:31,253 --> 00:22:32,083
I hear you.

313
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:37,117
My heart's at a time

314
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,737
Thank

315
00:22:38,820 --> 00:22:45,820
you.

316
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:12,777
My world's true if we're in a dream.

317
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:16,540
Even if we're in trouble,

318
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:20,220
but in the deep end,

319
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:25,460
I'm always, always playing.

320
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:31,420
I'm slowly, slowly, shining.

321
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:38,740
Crimson killing intent.
